{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q423721","formula":"C₂H₄OS","hill":"C2H4OS","elements":["H","C","O","S"],"composition":{"C":2.0,"H":4.0,"O":1.0,"S":1.0},"names":{"en":"Thioacetic acid","ru":"Тиоуксусная кислота"},"descriptions":{"en":"Thioacetic acid is an organosulfur compound with the molecular formula CH3C(O)SH. It is a thioic acid: the sulfur analogue of acetic acid (CH3C(O)OH), as implied by the thio- prefix. It is a yellow liquid with a strong thiol-like odor. It is used in organic synthesis for the introduction of thiol groups (−SH) in molecules.","ru":"Тиоуксусная кислота — сераорганическое соединение с молекулярной формулой CH3COSH. Представляет собой жидкость жёлтого цвета с сильным тиоловым запахом. Используется в органическом синтезе для введения тиильных групп в молекулы, а также для получения тиолов."},"fame":22,"pubchemCid":10484,"mass":76.12,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC(=O)S","inchikey":"DUYAAUVXQSMXQP-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"ethanethioic S-acid","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"10484","atoms":8,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":1.613,"y":-0.281,"z":0.0,"el":"S"},{"x":-0.502,"y":1.263,"z":0.0,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.009,"y":-1.089,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.102,"y":0.107,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.84,"y":-1.693,"z":-0.896,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.842,"y":-1.69,"z":0.898,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.05,"y":-0.752,"z":-0.002,"el":"H"},{"x":2.063,"y":0.982,"z":0.0,"el":"H"}],"bonds":[[0,3,1],[0,7,1],[1,3,2],[2,3,1],[2,4,1],[2,5,1],[2,6,1]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q423721","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thioacetic_acid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%A2%D0%B8%D0